    {"brand":"Apple","match":"^iPhone","os_years":null,"security_years":5,"from":"launch","official":false,"note":"Apple makes no general update promise. Its only published commitment is the UK PSTI filing (e.g. iPhone 15 Pro Max) stating security updates for a 'minimum five years from the first supply date'. Historical pattern (not a promise): ~6-7 years of major iOS versions (iOS 26 supports 'iPhone 11 and later', dropping 2018's iPhone XS/XR after iOS 12-18) and security fixes for older iOS lines well beyond that (iOS 15.8.8 in May 2026 for iPhone 6s from 2015).","source":"https://support.apple.com/en-us/100100","source_secondary":"https://regulatoryinfo.apple.com/cwt/api/ext/file?fileId=securityTelecommunication%2FiPhone%2015%20Pro%20Max%20%28Model%20A3106%29_V0.pdf"},
    {"brand":"Apple","match":"^iPad","os_years":null,"security_years":null,"from":"launch","official":false,"note":"No official promise. Historical pattern only: iPadOS 26 supports iPad Pro 12.9-in (3rd gen, 2018)+, iPad Pro 11-in (1st gen, 2018)+, iPad Air (3rd gen, 2019)+, iPad (8th gen, 2020)+, iPad mini (5th gen, 2019)+, i.e. roughly 6-8 years of major iPadOS versions.","source":"https://support.apple.com/en-us/100100"},

